# Permanent continuous healthcheck — cron entry for the Coolify node(s).
#
# Cadence: EVERY 5 MINUTES (continuous), Europe/Berlin wall clock.
# This is deliberately frequent: unlike backups/ (daily dumps), a dead DB or
# app must page dev@ within minutes, not next day.
#
# Install (idempotent) with:  sudo ./monitors/install-coolify-healthcheck.sh <ssh-host>
# which writes this file to /etc/cron.d/coolify-healthcheck on the target node.
#
# Alternative: run the same script as a Coolify "Scheduled Task" on the node
# with schedule `*/5 * * * *` and command
# `/usr/local/sbin/coolify-healthcheck.sh` (env file must exist on that host).
#
# Tune: change */5 to */1 or */2 for 1–2 min cadence once SMTP is proven
# (watch alert + log volume first).

TZ=Europe/Berlin
*/5 * * * * root /usr/local/sbin/coolify-healthcheck.sh >> /var/log/coolify-healthcheck.log 2>&1
